1 | /* Loop 5 · DCF drift monitor (the continuous-monitoring control loop).
2 |  *
3 |  * Runs the SAME client DCF functions (src/dash/51_dcf.js) in Node against the embedded bases +
4 |  * external anchors, and records — per anchored name — the model fair value, the % gap to the anchor,
5 |  * whether a single plausible assumption reconciles them, and a FLAG when the gap exceeds tolerance
6 |  * AND nothing reconciles (the "model regressed or the thesis genuinely changed" signal).
7 |  *
8 |  * Pure/deterministic; no connector calls. Writes data/dcf_monitor.json and prints a one-line summary
9 |  * to stderr for the daily run report. This does NOT force anything — it only observes and flags.
10 |  *
11 |  * Usage:  node scripts/dcf_monitor.js            (DCF_DRIFT_TOL=% overrides the default 12% gate)
12 |  */
